  "changed_since_previous": "Added testing and validation for `-torpassword` authentication, ensuring the harness checks that Tor receives the password unescaped and only after offering HASHEDPASSWORD authentication.",
  "card": "Rewrites the torcontrol fuzz target to route traffic through a mocked DynSock connection to a simulated Tor daemon rather than invoking TorController callbacks directly. The simulated Tor answers commands with valid wire replies for PROTOCOLINFO, SAFECOOKIE challenges, GETINFO, and ADD_ONION, while verifying that the controller only uses offered auth methods, uses fresh nonces, preserves passwords, and advertises the correct onion service. It also fixes a bug in the DynSock::Wait test utility where sockets deleted themselves. The author reports that line coverage on src/torcontrol.cpp increases from 52% to 81% and that the target can reproduce the escaping bug fixed in #36637 within a few hundred runs.",
